{"id": "EUVD-2026-108863", "enisaUuid": "547533d4-b384-31cc-973c-f00f3943b11c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: protect sb_write_pointer() with invalidate lock\n\nsb_write_pointer() reads the super block from the block device page cache\nusing read_cache_page_gfp(). This has the same race with BLKBSZSET as the\none fixed by commit 3f29d661e568 (\"btrfs: sync read disk super and set\nblock size\").\n\nTake the mapping invalidate lock around read_cache_page_gfp() to\nserialize the read against block size changes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9b38f2eab5a9bd74087390318d93ccdd8d2deff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0dc28359a8a26f970ccd250b126a2e0bd4118a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a6c92aa7242a04e4349c0ea213dbf703a1c9891", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a58cab4535f085adc0f93d7efd7952ef437371da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80cd97c5e90096d040a623851795eac92fbd0ff1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/123b9a545f4d0348e81f558a032bf2a93ee5722f", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98907"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2r98-r7qj-j43v", "CVE-2026-98907"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a29d378-cf1f-3923-8d54-f47beeeb5210", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "114198a2-5d69-3ae8-abe1-1340252e0a1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <5.15.222"}, {"id": "14f5bf48-a45b-30af-9bfd-a5b05bb71d7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <80cd97c5e90096d040a623851795eac92fbd0ff1"}, {"id": "29a3015b-42f2-3c61-8a27-c56c308a37dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "2a66f672-9ded-325d-a30d-1a6e7bbf05d6", "product"